# The bump paths store pointers and lengths through uint8_t * budgets and
# read MethodTable fields through narrower casts. The bytes model loses a
# pointer stored in memory (it keeps the integer only), so the typed model
# with casts is used; it checks those accesses per memory cell, and the
# byte extent of each object is stated separately (the bump behaviors'
# \valid ensures).
-wp-model Typed+cast
# The runtime's helpers and the ZkvmThrow handler have footprints this
# module cannot state: no generated assigns, so WP assumes they write
# anything.
-generated-spec-custom assigns:skip
# (v & ~7) >= v - 7: no prover gets the bit fact.
-wp-prop=-round_down_8
-wp-prover alt-ergo,z3,cvc4
